    <task><title>Part 2 - 1 point</title>
<statement><p>The results from the table indicate the two-sided limit of <m>\displaystyle{ \lim_{x \to 4} {4-3x}}</m> is <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0007"/>  (if the two-sided limit does not exist, type in DNE).</p>
</statement><hint><p>Recall, the two sided limit exists if and only if both one sided limits exist and are equal. In other words,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\lim_{x\rightarrow a} f(x)}</m> exists and is equal to <m>L</m> if and only if <m>\displaystyle{\lim_{x\rightarrow a^+} f(x)=\lim_{x\rightarrow a^-} f(x) = L}</m></p>
</hint><answer><p><m>-8</m></p></answer></task>
